      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": { "id": "title" },
      "source": [
        "# EEEM004 MSc Project — SAM Audio Separation Pipeline\n",
        "**Automated Soundtrack Personalisation for Neurodivergent Listeners Using Generative AI**\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "**Student:** Louis Ilett  \n",
        "**Supervisor:** Prof Philip Jackson  \n",
        "**Module:** EEEM004 — MSc Project, University of Surrey\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Overview\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook implements the source separation stage of the soundtrack personalisation pipeline using **Meta SAM Audio** — a foundation model for general audio separation that accepts natural language text prompts to isolate any sound from a mixture.\n",
        "\n",
        "Unlike the previous Demucs-based approach (which separated into fixed stems: vocals/drums/bass/other), SAM Audio allows direct prompting for project-relevant categories:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Prompt | Purpose |\n",
        "|--------|---------|\n",
        "| `\"a person speaking\"` | Isolate dialogue |\n",
        "| `\"background music\"` | Isolate music bed |\n",
        "| `\"sound effects\"` | Isolate SFX/ambience |\n",
        "\n",
        "Each separation produces two outputs:\n",
        "- **`result.target`** — the isolated sound matching the prompt\n",
        "- **`result.residual`** — everything else (the remainder of the mix)\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Prerequisites:**\n",
        "> - Runtime set to **T4 GPU** (Runtime > Change runtime type > T4 GPU)\n",
        "> - Hugging Face access approved at huggingface.co/facebook/sam-audio-large\n",
        "> - HF token saved in Colab Secrets as `HF_TOKEN`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": { "id": "setup_header" },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 1. Setup & Installation\n",
        "\n",
        "Installs SAM Audio directly from the Meta GitHub repository, along with supporting libraries.\n",
        "\n",
        "**After this cell completes, restart the runtime** (Runtime > Restart runtime) before continuing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": { "id": "install" },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Install SAM Audio from Meta's GitHub repo\n",
        "!pip install git+https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam-audio.git --quiet\n",
        "\n",
        "# Supporting libraries\n",
        "!pip install torchaudio librosa soundfile matplotlib yt-dlp --quiet\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Installation complete. Please restart the runtime before running the next cell.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": { "id": "imports_header" },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 2. Imports & GPU Check\n",
        "\n",
        "Run after restarting the runtime. Also confirms the T4 GPU is active and checks available VRAM (need ~14GB for the large model)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": { "id": "imports" },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import os\n",
        "import torch\n",
        "import torchaudio\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import librosa\n",
        "import librosa.display\n",
        "import soundfile as sf\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from IPython.display import Audio, display\n",
        "from sam_audio import SAMAudio, SAMAudioProcessor\n",
        "\n",
        "# Check GPU\n",
        "device = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
        "print(f\"Device: {device}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
        "    gpu_name = torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)\n",
        "    vram_gb = torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory / 1e9\n",
        "    print(f\"GPU: {gpu_name}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"VRAM: {vram_gb:.1f} GB\")\n",
        "    if vram_gb < 13:\n",
        "        print(\"WARNING: Less than 13GB VRAM detected. Consider using sam-audio-small instead of sam-audio-large.\")\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        print(\"VRAM sufficient for sam-audio-large.\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"WARNING: No GPU detected. Go to Runtime > Change runtime type > T4 GPU.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": { "id": "auth_header" },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 3. Authentication\n",
        "\n",
        "SAM Audio is a gated model and requires a Hugging Face token.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Do not paste your token directly into the code.** Instead:\n",
        "1. Click the 🔑 **Secrets** tab in the left sidebar\n",
        "2. Add a new secret named `HF_TOKEN` with your token as the value\n",
        "3. Run the cell below to load it securely\n",
        "\n",
        "If you haven't been approved yet, visit huggingface.co/facebook/sam-audio-large to request access."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": { "id": "auth" },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from google.colab import userdata\n",
        "\n",
        "HF_TOKEN = userdata.get('HF_TOKEN')\n",
        "\n",
        "if HF_TOKEN:\n",
        "    # Authenticate so the model can be downloaded\n",
        "    from huggingface_hub import login\n",
        "    login(token=HF_TOKEN, add_to_git_credential=False)\n",
        "    print(\"Hugging Face authentication successful.\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"WARNING: HF_TOKEN not found in Colab Secrets. Add it via the key icon in the left sidebar.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": { "id": "download_header" },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 4. Audio Acquisition\n",
        "\n",
        "Download audio from YouTube. SAM Audio works best with WAV format.\n",
        "\n",
        "**For this project, choose a clip with a mix of dialogue, music, and/or sound effects.** Good options:\n",
        "- A podcast episode or clip\n",
        "- A film or TV scene with dialogue over music\n",
        "- A documentary with narration and background sound\n",
        "\n",
        "Keep the clip under 3 minutes for reasonable processing time on Colab."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": { "id": "download" },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "YOUTUBE_URL = \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YOUR_VIDEO_ID\"  # <-- replace this\n",
        "INPUT_PATH = \"/content/input_audio.wav\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Downloading from: {YOUTUBE_URL}\")\n",
        "!yt-dlp -x --audio-format wav --audio-quality 0 -o \"{INPUT_PATH}\" \"{YOUTUBE_URL}\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Check duration\n",
        "y_check, sr_check = librosa.load(INPUT_PATH, sr=None, mono=True)\n",
        "duration = len(y_check) / sr_check\n",
        "print(f\"\\nDownloaded: {duration:.1f} seconds at {sr_check} Hz\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if duration > 180:\n",
        "    print(\"WARNING: Clip is over 3 minutes. Consider trimming for faster processing.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nPlaying original audio:\")\n",
        "display(Audio(INPUT_PATH))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": { "id": "trim_header" },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 5. (Optional) Trim Audio\n",
        "\n",
        "If your clip is long, trim it to a manageable segment. Skip this cell if it is already under 2 minutes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": { "id": "trim" },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "START_SEC = 0    # start time in seconds\n",
        "END_SEC = 90     # end time in seconds — adjust as needed\n",
        "\n",
        "TRIMMED_PATH = \"/content/input_trimmed.wav\"\n",
        "\n",
        "y_full, sr_full = librosa.load(INPUT_PATH, sr=None, mono=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "start_sample = int(START_SEC * sr_full)\n",
        "end_sample = int(END_SEC * sr_full)\n",
        "\n",
        "if y_full.ndim == 1:\n",
        "    y_trimmed = y_full[start_sample:end_sample]\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    y_trimmed = y_full[:, start_sample:end_sample]\n",
        "\n",
        "sf.write(TRIMMED_PATH, y_trimmed.T if y_trimmed.ndim > 1 else y_trimmed, sr_full)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Use trimmed file as input going forward\n",
        "INPUT_PATH = TRIMMED_PATH\n",
        "print(f\"Trimmed to {END_SEC - START_SEC}s. Playing trimmed audio:\")\n",
        "display(Audio(INPUT_PATH))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": { "id": "model_header" },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 6. Load SAM Audio Model\n",
        "\n",
        "Downloads and loads the `sam-audio-large` model (~14GB VRAM). This will take a few minutes the first time as the weights are downloaded from Hugging Face.\n",
        "\n",
        "If you run into VRAM issues, replace `sam-audio-large` with `sam-audio-small`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": { "id": "load_model" },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "MODEL_ID = \"facebook/sam-audio-large\"  # or \"facebook/sam-audio-small\" if VRAM is tight\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Loading {MODEL_ID}...\")\n",
        "print(\"(This may take a few minutes on first run while weights download)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "model = SAMAudio.from_pretrained(MODEL_ID).to(device).eval()\n",
        "processor = SAMAudioProcessor.from_pretrained(MODEL_ID)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\nModel loaded successfully on {device}.\")\n",
        "print(f\"Audio sample rate: {processor.audio_sampling_rate} Hz\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": { "id": "separation_header" },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 7. Text-Prompted Source Separation\n",
        "\n",
        "This is the core stage. SAM Audio is prompted with natural language descriptions to isolate specific sounds.\n",
        "\n",
        "Three separations are run — one for each project-relevant category:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Prompt | Target category |\n",
        "|--------|-----------------|\n",
        "| `\"a person speaking\"` | Dialogue / speech |\n",
        "| `\"background music\"` | Music bed |\n",
        "| `\"sound effects and ambient noise\"` | SFX / ambience |\n",
        "\n",
        "Each call returns:\n",
        "- **`result.target`** — the isolated sound\n",
        "- **`result.residual`** — everything else\n",
        "\n",
        "`predict_spans=True` lets the model automatically detect where in the audio the target sound occurs, improving separation quality."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": { "id": "separation" },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Define the prompts for each category\n",
        "SEPARATIONS = {\n",
        "    \"dialogue\": \"a person speaking\",\n",
        "    \"music\":    \"background music\",\n",
        "    \"sfx\":      \"sound effects and ambient noise\",\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR = \"/content/sam_output\"\n",
        "os.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "results = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for category, prompt in SEPARATIONS.items():\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nSeparating: '{prompt}'...\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Process inputs\n",
        "    inputs = processor(\n",
        "        audios=[INPUT_PATH],\n",
        "        descriptions=[prompt]\n",
        "    ).to(device)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Run separation\n",
        "    with torch.inference_mode():\n",
        "        result = model.separate(inputs, predict_spans=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Save target and residual\n",
        "    target_path   = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, f\"{category}_target.wav\")\n",
        "    residual_path = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, f\"{category}_residual.wav\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    torchaudio.save(target_path,   result.target[0].unsqueeze(0).cpu(),   processor.audio_sampling_rate)\n",
        "    torchaudio.save(residual_path, result.residual[0].unsqueeze(0).cpu(), processor.audio_sampling_rate)\n",
        "\n",
        "    results[category] = {\n",
        "        \"prompt\":   prompt,\n",
        "        \"target\":   target_path,\n",
        "        \"residual\": residual_path\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(f\"  Saved: {target_path}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  Saved: {residual_path}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nAll separations complete.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": { "id": "listen_header" },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 8. Listen to Separation Results\n",
        "\n",
        "Play back each separated stem alongside its residual. Key things to listen for:\n",
        "- How cleanly is the target sound isolated?\n",
        "- What bleeds into the target that shouldn't be there?\n",
        "- Does the residual sound like everything except the target?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": { "id": "listen" },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"=\" * 50)\n",
        "print(\"ORIGINAL MIXTURE\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 50)\n",
        "display(Audio(INPUT_PATH))\n",
        "\n",
        "for category, data in results.items():\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n{'=' * 50}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"PROMPT: '{data['prompt']}'\")\n",
        "    print(f\"{'=' * 50}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Target (isolated {category}):\")\n",
        "    display(Audio(data[\"target\"]))\n",
        "    print(f\"Residual (everything else):\")\n",
        "    display(Audio(data[\"residual\"]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": { "id": "reconstruction_header" },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 9. Personalised Mix Reconstruction\n",
        "\n",
        "This cell demonstrates the personalisation concept central to the project.\n",
        "\n",
        "Using the separated dialogue stem, a modified mix is created with:\n",
        "- **Dialogue boosted** (increased volume)\n",
        "- **Background reduced** (decreased volume)\n",
        "\n",
        "This represents the kind of accessible remix that might benefit a neurodivergent listener who finds background sounds distracting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": { "id": "reconstruction" },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "DIALOGUE_BOOST = 1.5   # multiply dialogue volume by this factor\n",
        "BACKGROUND_REDUCE = 0.3  # multiply background volume by this factor\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load dialogue target and residual\n",
        "dialogue_target,   sr_d = librosa.load(results[\"dialogue\"][\"target\"],   sr=None, mono=True)\n",
        "dialogue_residual, sr_r = librosa.load(results[\"dialogue\"][\"residual\"], sr=None, mono=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Align lengths\n",
        "min_len = min(len(dialogue_target), len(dialogue_residual))\n",
        "dialogue_target   = dialogue_target[:min_len]\n",
        "dialogue_residual = dialogue_residual[:min_len]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create personalised mix\n",
        "personalised_mix = (dialogue_target * DIALOGUE_BOOST) + (dialogue_residual * BACKGROUND_REDUCE)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Normalise to prevent clipping\n",
        "personalised_mix = personalised_mix / np.max(np.abs(personalised_mix))\n",
        "\n",
        "PERSONALISED_PATH = \"/content/personalised_mix.wav\"\n",
        "sf.write(PERSONALISED_PATH, personalised_mix, sr_d)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Personalised mix: dialogue x{DIALOGUE_BOOST}, background x{BACKGROUND_REDUCE}\")\n",
        "print(\"\\nOriginal mixture:\")\n",
        "display(Audio(INPUT_PATH))\n",
        "print(\"\\nPersonalised mix (dialogue boosted, background reduced):\")\n",
        "display(Audio(PERSONALISED_PATH))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": { "id": "viz_header" },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 10. Spectrogram Visualisation\n",
        "\n",
        "Plots spectrograms of the original mixture, each separated target stem, and the personalised mix. Useful for visually confirming what frequency content has been isolated."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": { "id": "visualisation" },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Build list of signals to plot\n",
        "plot_signals = [(INPUT_PATH, \"Original Mixture\")]\n",
        "for category, data in results.items():\n",
        "    label = f\"SAM Audio — {category.capitalize()} target ('{data['prompt']}')\"\n",
        "    plot_signals.append((data[\"target\"], label))\n",
        "plot_signals.append((PERSONALISED_PATH, f\"Personalised Mix (dialogue x{DIALOGUE_BOOST}, background x{BACKGROUND_REDUCE})\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(len(plot_signals), 1, figsize=(14, 4 * len(plot_signals)))\n",
        "fig.suptitle(\"Spectrogram Comparison — SAM Audio Separation Pipeline\",\n",
        "             fontsize=13, fontweight=\"bold\", y=1.01)\n",
        "\n",
        "for ax, (path, title) in zip(axes, plot_signals):\n",
        "    y_sig, sr_sig = librosa.load(path, sr=None, mono=True)\n",
        "    y_sig = y_sig[:sr_sig * 60]  # cap at 60s for display\n",
        "    D = librosa.amplitude_to_db(np.abs(librosa.stft(y_sig)), ref=np.max)\n",
        "    img = librosa.display.specshow(D, sr=sr_sig, x_axis=\"time\", y_axis=\"log\", ax=ax)\n",
        "    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=10)\n",
        "    ax.set_ylabel(\"Frequency (Hz)\")\n",
        "    fig.colorbar(img, ax=ax, format=\"%+2.0f dB\")\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[-1].set_xlabel(\"Time (s)\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.savefig(\"/content/sam_spectrograms.png\", dpi=150, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "print(\"Saved to /content/sam_spectrograms.png\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": { "id": "comparison_header" },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 11. Comparison with Previous Approach (Demucs)\n",
        "\n",
        "This section documents the key differences between the Demucs-based pipeline and the SAM Audio pipeline for the purposes of Objective 4 of the project (comparing AI-based approaches with simpler methods).\n",
        "\n",
        "| Aspect | Demucs (previous) | SAM Audio (current) |\n",
        "|--------|-------------------|---------------------|\n",
        "| **Prompt type** | Fixed stems (vocals/drums/bass/other) | Free-text natural language |\n",
        "| **Dialogue isolation** | Indirect (vocals stem approximation) | Direct (`\"a person speaking\"`) |\n",
        "| **Music/SFX separation** | Not supported | Directly prompted |\n",
        "| **Architecture** | Hybrid spectrogram/waveform U-Net | Flow-matching diffusion transformer |\n",
        "| **Flexibility** | Low — fixed output categories | High — any sound can be targeted |\n",
        "| **VRAM requirement** | ~4GB | ~14GB (large model) |"
      ]
    },
    {
